sePath, session, kind)`:\n\nFor a plain object/array:\n```ts\nfunction makeProxy(value, basePath, session, kind) {\n  if (value === null || typeof value !== 'object') return value\n  return new Proxy(value, {\n    get(target, prop, receiver) {\n      if (prop === Symbol.toStringTag || prop === 'then') return Reflect.get(target, prop, receiver)\n      if (typeof prop === 'symbol') return Reflect.get(target, prop, receiver)\n      const key = String(prop)\n      // array methods\n      if (Array.isArray(target) && key === 'includes') {\n        // record all indices\n        for (let i = 0; i < target.length; i++) {\n          record(session, basePath, String(i), kind)\n        }\n        return target.includes.bind(target)\n      }\n      if (key === 'length') {\n        record(session, basePath, '', kind, true) // whole\n        return target.length\n      }\n      const result = Reflect.get(target, prop, receiver)\n      // Map/Set methods handled at Map/Set proxy level, not here\n      const childPath = joinPath(basePath, key)\n      record(session, childPath, kind)\n      if (typeof result === 'object' && result !== null) {\n        return makeProxy(result, childPath, session, kind)\n      }\n      return result\n    },\n    has(target, prop) {\n      const key = String(prop)\n      record(session, joinPath(basePath, key), kind)\n      return Reflect.has(target, prop)\n    },\n    ownKeys() { /* maybe not needed */ }\n  })\n}\n```\n\nBut for arrays, `includes` is a method on the array. When `func` calls `list.includes('x')`, the get trap for `'includes'` returns `target.includes.bind(target)` \u2014 but we need to also track elements checked. Since `includes` iterates the array internally with native code, we can't intercept element reads. So we record all indices in the get trap. Good.\n\nFor Map:\n```ts\nfunction makeMapProxy(value, basePath, session, kind) {\n  return new Proxy(value, {\n    get(target, prop, receiver) {\n      if (prop === 'get' || prop === '