add(p)`.\n\nLet's implement:\n```ts\ntype Recorder = (path: string) => void\n\nfunction createProxy(value: any, basePath: string, recorder: Recorder): any {\n  if (value === null || typeof value !== 'object') return value\n  if (value instanceof Map) return createMapProxy(value, basePath, recorder)\n  if (value instanceof Set) return createSetProxy(value, basePath, recorder)\n  return createObjectProxy(value, basePath, recorder)\n}\n```\n\nObject proxy:\n```ts\nfunction createObjectProxy(value, basePath, recorder) {\n  return new Proxy(value, {\n    get(target, prop, receiver) {\n      if (typeof prop === 'symbol') {\n        return Reflect.get(target, prop, receiver)\n      }\n      const key = String(prop)\n      if (Array.isArray(target) && key === 'includes') {\n        for (let i = 0; i < target.length; i++) recorder(joinPath(basePath, String(i)))\n        return target.includes.bind(target)\n      }\n      if (key === 'length') {\n        recorder(basePath) // whole\n        return target.length\n      }\n      const result = Reflect.get(target, prop, receiver)\n      const childPath = joinPath(basePath, key)\n      recorder(childPath)\n      if (typeof result === 'object' && result !== null) {\n        return createProxy(result, childPath, recorder)\n      }\n      return result\n    },\n    has(target, prop) {\n      const key = String(prop)\n      recorder(joinPath(basePath, key))\n      return Reflect.has(target, prop)\n    }\n  })\n}\n```\n\nBut there's an issue: if we record `user.name` on the selector proxy, and then the func accesses `user.name.length` (string length), our object proxy's get trap for `'length'` would call `recorder(basePath)` which records `user.name` (whole) \u2014 that's the desired fallback for primitives? Actually `user.name` is a string, so `createProxy` returns the primitive string itself (not proxy). Then accessing `.length` on a primitive string goes through String wrapper, not our proxy, so no recording. The dep remains `user.